11
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:26,260
I...

12
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:31,520
I'm going to avenge Archer.

13
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:34,140
In spite of everything,

14
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:38,780
he was still my partner.

15
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,340
Same here.

16
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,850
I've made up my mind to fight.

17
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:50,410
If I didn't see this through till the end, he'd never let me hear the end of it.

18
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:54,090
Plus, we can't just leave the Grail be.

19
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:56,510
It needs to be destroyed.

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,880
I agree.

21
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:06,600
A miracle that gathers the wishes of all but accepts only one

22
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,800
should never have existed.

23
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:10,930
Saber...

24
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:14,450
But would you be okay with that, Rin?

25
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:17,730
Is it not the cherished dream of the Tohsaka family to win the Grail?

26
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:22,030
It is, but I don't want some monkey's paw of a weapon.

27
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:26,090
I never really had a wish I wanted granted, anyway.

28
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:29,280
And smashing it will be cathartic in its own way.

29
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:36,160
I didn't enter the Holy Grail War for the spoils. Only to win.

30
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:40,670
To hold my head high as a Tohsaka.

31
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,540
Yeah.

32
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:43,880
That sounds like you.

33
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,320
What do you mean, it sounds like me?

34
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,500
It hardly even makes sense!

35
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:50,390
All right.

36
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,220
Sh-Shirou?

37
00:01:52,730 --> 00:01:54,060
Wh-What?

38
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:57,220
Oh, I figured I'd make us something to eat.

39
00:01:57,220 --> 00:01:59,150
You two must be hungry.

40
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:02,020
Haste makes waste, right?

41
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:06,240
Let's start by filling our bellies and considering our options.

42
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,900
Yes, that is true.

43
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:11,160
Let's have dinner as usual.

44
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:14,160
That's how we've always done things.

45
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,350
I guess you're right.

46
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:19,670
Okay, I'll help out.

