10380
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:57,510
{\an4}A Winter's Day, A Long Way Home

10381
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:57,510
{\an4}A Winter's Day, A Long Way Home

10382
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:57,510
{\an4}A Winter's Day, A Long Way Home

10383
00:04:12,370 --> 00:04:14,660
The Holy Grail is at Ryuudou Temple?

10384
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,410
Yes.

10385
00:04:15,410 --> 00:04:18,790
There are three places in town 
where the Grail can be manifested.

10386
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:20,410
My home,

10387
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:22,120
Kirei's church,

10388
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,190
and Ryuudou Temple on Mt. Enzou.

10389
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:29,630
I sent familiars to each, and the one at Ryuudou Temple was smashed.

10390
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:34,260
It's safe to assume that flashy gold jerk is setting up camp at Ryuudou Temple.

10391
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:37,300
Doesn't that mean Issei and the others there are in danger?

10392
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,420
Look at this.

10393
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:43,310
Gas leak accident?!

10394
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:43,310
５２　ＵＮＣＯＮＳＣＩＯＵＳ

10395
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:43,310
Everyone there was taken away in ambulances?

10396
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:44,510
Right.

10397
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:47,510
This means that any interlopers have been removed ahead of time.

10398
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:49,330
Shinji's doing, no doubt.

10399
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,430
It's the kind of move I'd expect a wary guy like him to make,

10400
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:53,930
but in this case, it's a godsend.

10401
00:04:55,710 --> 00:04:59,080
Ryuudou Temple, though... That will prove problematic.

10402
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,600
With its anti-spirit barrier,

10403
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:05,080
Servants can only enter through the main gate.

10404
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:09,040
On the upside, knowing exactly where the Grail will be is good for us.

10405
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:12,340
After all, our first priority is to stop its summoning.

10406
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:14,410
Saber will take the main gate.

10407
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:17,280
She'll keep him occupied out front,

10408
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:21,470
and as she does, we'll climb the mountain from the back and destroy the Grail.

10409
00:05:21,470 --> 00:05:22,470
Hang on...

10410
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:26,490
Isn't Saber the only one who can destroy it?

10411
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,480
Good point.

10412
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:32,790
Once the Grail's summoned, we won't be able to destroy it.

10413
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:36,940
But we can destroy its vessel before then.

10414
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:40,990
Basically, we shut down the Grail before it can activate.

10415
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,110
What do you mean?

10416
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,450
Judging by the events up until now,

10417
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:48,250
you would assume the Holy Grail is Illyasviel's heart, right?

10418
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:51,320
But I think it also needs her body—

10419
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:54,510
or rather, magic circuits—to function.

10420
00:05:54,510 --> 00:05:58,130
He didn't want Illyasviel to become the Grail,

10421
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:01,140
so he only removed the core: her heart.

10422
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:05,130
Therefore, for it to function,

10423
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:08,340
he needs to implant it into another mage's body.

10424
00:06:09,180 --> 00:06:10,900
Since the two of us are here,

10425
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:13,630
his choice for the Grail's foundation has to be...

10426
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,000
Shinji?

10427
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,030
But he isn't, well...

10428
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:23,540
Even if the Matou mage lineage has died out, 
they still have latent magic circuits.

10429
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:28,510
Illyasviel's heart would forcibly open even those.

10430
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:33,300
Which means that we have to start by locating Shinji.

10431
00:06:33,790 --> 00:06:39,550
Then I need to distract Archer until you two stop the Grail?

10432
00:06:39,550 --> 00:06:40,800
Yes.

10433
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:44,160
And as soon as we stop the Grail, we'll come running.

10434
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,950
No, that's crazy.

10435
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:47,930
Saber's no match for him.

10436
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:51,010
On what grounds do you base that assessment, Shirou?

10437
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:57,030
Uh... As a swordsman, he's no match for you,

10438
00:06:57,370 --> 00:07:01,740
but no matter how skilled the warrior, they can't defeat war itself.

10439
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:04,280
He's that kind of Heroic Spirit.

10440
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:08,820
You also have to be war itself, or you'll be swallowed whole.

10441
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:13,040
So you are saying that I would be at a disadvantage against him?

10442
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:21,060
That's why we can't send Saber to fight him without a plan, Tohsaka.

10443
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:23,300
We need to figure out his weakness, at least.

10444
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:28,000
Like you said, his Noble Phantasm is war itself,

10445
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,480
and on top of that, he's a Servant specialized in killing Heroic Spirits.

10446
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:36,490
To beat him, you'd need to have an armory to equal his...

10447
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:43,500
What?

10448
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,530
Why did you stop mid-sentence?

10449
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:48,120
I see.

10450
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:51,140
That's why he always treated him like a sworn enemy.

10451
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:55,130
Right, a Heroic Spirit without his own Noble Phantasm

10452
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:58,260
wouldn't have an original weapon.

10453
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:00,120
It'll work...

10454
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,130
This will work!

10455
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:06,810
Hang on, that would mean...

10456
00:08:06,810 --> 00:08:09,450
If you have something to say, spit it out.

10457
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:11,350
You have an idea, right?

10458
00:08:11,350 --> 00:08:13,250
I do not!

10459
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:16,020
I can't tell you here, you idiot!

10460
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:19,030
Rin?

10461
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:22,490
Anyway, the existing plan should be fine.

10462
00:08:22,490 --> 00:08:24,470
We carry it out before dawn, got it?

10463
00:08:24,470 --> 00:08:28,670
Until then, everyone should go to their rooms and get plenty of rest.

10464
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:34,580
Also, I need to discuss something with you, Saber.

10465
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:45,640
You're okay with this, Saber?

10466
00:08:47,350 --> 00:08:49,850
Yes. I think it the best option.

10467
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,700
You have my thanks, Rin.

10468
00:08:53,190 --> 00:08:56,230
This will allow me to fight without undue concern as well.

10469
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,370
What do you want?

10470
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,640
What do I...

10471
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:15,370
Did I catch you in a really bad mood or something?

10472
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:19,450
No, not really. It's not like that.

10473
00:09:19,450 --> 00:09:21,020
What's your problem, then?

10474
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:23,320
Do you have a fever or something?

10475
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,570
Of course I don't!

10476
00:09:24,570 --> 00:09:27,750
Jeez... Just come in already.

10477
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:30,250
Let me guess, you're here for another stupid reason?

10478
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:42,460
Tohsaka, what were you and Saber...

10479
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:43,950
What?

10480
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:45,650
No, forget it.

10481
00:09:46,730 --> 00:09:49,180
Just hear me out and don't get mad.

10482
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,410
I want to—

10483
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:52,540
You want to fight him, don't you?

10484
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:58,330
Oh? So you figured it out.

10485
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:02,670
That the natural enemy of Gilgamesh's Noble Phantasm is Archer's magic.

10486
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:04,650
It is?

10487
00:10:04,650 --> 00:10:06,700
Huh? Hang on...

10488
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:10,760
You came up with that hare-brained suggestion without even figuring that much out?

10489
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:15,890
No, I just had a gut feeling that I'd have the best chance out of the three of us.

10490
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,860
Well, your gut isn't wrong.

10491
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:24,560
What makes Gilgamesh the most powerful is the 
overwhelming number of Noble Phantasms he has.

10492
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,940
Furthermore, for every anti-Heroic-Spirit weapon there is, he has the original.

10493
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:32,020
But there is no Noble Phantasm legendary for killing Archer.

10494
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:36,810
Most of all, given sufficient mana, 
he could match anyone weapon for weapon.

10495
00:10:38,310 --> 00:10:42,140
Gilgamesh called you two "fakes,"

10496
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:46,000
but I'll bet that was because he actually saw you as threats.

10497
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,760
Because unlike others, he would have to fight Heroic Spirit Emiya on equal footing.

10498
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,880
There's a flaw in your plan, though.

10499
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:56,810
My projections won't be able to keep up with his barrage of Noble Phantasms,

10500
00:10:56,810 --> 00:10:58,430
and my mana won't last.

10501
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:02,200
Yes, if your magic stays at its current level.

10502
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:05,490
But you remember Archer's Noble Phantasm, right?

10503
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:06,940
If you could master that magic—

10504
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:12,450
that Reality Marble—you could hold your own against Gilgamesh.

10505
00:11:12,450 --> 00:11:13,920
That's crazy.

10506
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,790
I don't have that kind of mana.

10507
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:19,660
Well, several options come to mind.

10508
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,960
But the one I'm thinking of...

10509
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:26,400
is a method that links two mages, along with their stores of mana.

10510
00:11:32,070 --> 00:11:36,260
You mean creating a path between you and me to share mana?

10511
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,070
Yes.

10512
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:41,810
Even if you don't have the mana to use a Reality Marble, I do.

10513
00:11:42,590 --> 00:11:47,050
I'll have you use my mana to fight Gilgamesh.

10514
00:11:48,070 --> 00:11:50,860
Now, as for how to establish that path...

10515
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:55,610
Tohsaka?

10516
00:12:01,070 --> 00:12:04,710
I'm going to transplant my magic crest onto you.

10517
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:07,980
But isn't that...

10518
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:11,710
Isn't the magic crest considered a mage's ultimate legacy?

10519
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:13,300
That's right.

10520
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:19,070
The current family head takes magic that was originally formless and shapes it over the course of their life.

10521
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:22,600
It's the heritage of a mage family, 
handed down from generation to generation.

10522
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:26,110
I can't take something that means so much to you.

10523
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:28,490
It's fine.

10524
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:30,670
This is my most important fight,

10525
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:33,110
so I have to commit my most important possession, right?

10526
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:38,620
Why are you staring at me like that?

10527
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:41,720
Sorry. I was just in awe of you for a second.

10528
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:46,790
I know it's kinda late to say this, 
but that's what made me fall for you.

10529
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:49,040
F-Fall for me?

10530
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:52,090
This is hardly the time for sweet talk!

10531
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:55,720
But if you want to keep going, 
I guess I could force myself to listen.

10532
00:12:56,250 --> 00:12:58,060
Yeah, I know.

10533
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,470
There's not much time.

10534
00:13:00,310 --> 00:13:02,800
Okay, let's start the transplant.

10535
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,560
What do you need me to do, Tohsaka?

10536
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:11,900
Well, start by getting undressed...

10537
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:18,910
What's wrong?

10538
00:13:18,910 --> 00:13:21,630
Look, don't get any funny ideas!

10539
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:24,660
I only said to take your clothes off, got it?

10540
00:13:24,660 --> 00:13:27,540
I'm taking mine off too, so it's all fair.

10541
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:30,380
You're undressing too?

10542
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:33,420
L-Like I said, don't get the wrong idea!

10543
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:36,630
Getting undressed is to facilitate the transfer of body heat.

10544
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:38,910
That's all there is to it!

10545
00:13:38,910 --> 00:13:41,920
Listen. To transplant a magic crest,

10546
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,860
we need to enter a state of deep rapport.

10547
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:46,770
Oh, I get it.

10548
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,650
Um, just my top is okay, right?

10549
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,150


10550
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:54,280
Obviously!

10551
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,300
I'm going to begin.

10552
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:21,900
Gib dem wandernden Vogel das Trinkwasser,

10553
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:21,900
Give to the migrating bird water,

10554
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:24,170
der vom langen Weg kommt.

10555
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:24,170
who hails from the long path.

10556
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:26,040
Benutz den Vogelrahmen

10557
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:26,040
Use the bird frame

10558
00:14:27,190 --> 00:14:31,030
in dem der Schlüssel nicht angewendet wird.

10559
00:14:27,190 --> 00:14:31,030
for which a key is not used.

10560
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:36,890
Ich spinne den Regenbogen in neuem selbst.

10561
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:36,890
I spin the rainbow anew.

10562
00:14:36,890 --> 00:14:39,200
Heißes Wetter, Regen,

10563
00:14:36,890 --> 00:14:39,200
Hot weather, rain,

10564
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:43,700
Wind, Schnee, Krieg, Ende, ununterbrochen.

10565
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:43,700
wind, snow, war, the end, repeat.

10566
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:49,710
Nimm an, ohne anderer Meinung zu sein, ohne zu fallen.

10567
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:49,710
Accept it without disagreeing, without falling.

10568
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:52,870
Es nimmt an, ohne zu fürchten,

10569
00:14:49,710 --> 00:14:52,870
It accepts it without fear

10570
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:54,960
ohne zu zweifeln.

10571
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:54,960
and without doubt.

10572
00:14:56,590 --> 00:15:02,140
Sieg im Freund, der auf eine Reise entfernt geht.

10573
00:14:56,590 --> 00:15:02,140
Victory to the friend on a long journey.

10574
00:16:44,990 --> 00:16:46,410
Tohsaka!

10575
00:16:49,350 --> 00:16:50,870
Did it work?

10576
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:55,630
Tohsaka?

10577
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:58,190
Of course it worked.

10578
00:16:58,190 --> 00:17:00,440
It was so flawless there's nothing to critique.

10579
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:03,220
So precise there won't be any aftereffects.

10580
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:05,960
So perfect that even Kirei, who specialized in this stuff,

10581
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:09,610
would compliment me and say, 
"That was fine work, my disciple."

10582
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,710
So this is...

10583
00:17:12,710 --> 00:17:13,780
Yes.

10584
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,480
It's the magic crest I transplanted onto you.

10585
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:20,850
This will give you more than enough mana to create a Reality Marble.

10586
00:17:20,850 --> 00:17:21,820
So the rest...

10587
00:17:22,490 --> 00:17:24,270
That's up to me.

10588
00:17:24,270 --> 00:17:26,200
Thanks, Tohsaka.

10589
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:32,200
But why are you so angry?

10590
00:17:33,690 --> 00:17:34,870
You saw it, didn't you?

10591
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:39,260
Hang on, did I do something?

10592
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,320
You saw it, didn't you? You brute!

10593
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,990
I don't know what you're talking about, but I'm sure you're wrong!

10594
00:17:44,990 --> 00:17:46,830
My eyes were closed the whole time,

10595
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:50,300
and the only thing I saw were some images that looked like magic circuits...

10596
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,820
